If a patient discontinues a naltrexone-treatment then every clinician should warn the patient about an overdose-risk from an opioid-use-resumption.
If a patient discontinues a naltrexone-treatment then the patient loses an opioid-dosage-tolerance.
If a patient loses an opioid-dosage-tolerance and the patient resumes an opioid-use then the opioid-use may cause an overdose-death for the patient.
